WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:11.199
if you have cancer [your] doctor may recommend

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:14.019
Chemotherapy as part of your treatment

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.420
The Cell's Nucleus controls this process

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:34.650
Inside each nucleus genetic material called Dna contains the instructions for directing this process

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.979
sometimes the cells Dna becomes damaged

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:48.369
Normally the DNa responds by either repairing itself or instructing the cell to die

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:56.419
in cancer however the parts of the cells Dna that [directs] cell division become damaged

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:04.169
When these sections are damaged the DnA is unable to repair itself or cause the cell to die

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:10.559
Instead the unrepaired Dna causes the cell to grow and divide uncontrollably

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.459
into more damaged cells called cancer cells

00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:22.938
a tumor forms as the cancer cells multiply and displace the normal cells

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.359
As the tumor enlarges it develops its own blood supply

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:46.480
Since cancer cells do not stick together as well as normal cells. They may break away and enter a nearby blood vessel

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:55.210
Cancer cells in blood vessels may travel to other areas of your body and form additional tumors. This is called Metastasis

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:59.560
additional tumors may form in areas such as the lungs

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.530
liver

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.800
and bones

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:12.330
Another way cancer may spread to other areas of your body is through your lymphatic system

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.030
cancer cells may enter Lymph vessels near the tumor

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.580
Then travel to small glands called Lymph nodes

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.579
if the cells pass through the nodes

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:35.190
They may continue to travel through your lymphatic system and form additional tumors

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:45.440
Chemotherapy drugs work by targeting fast-growing and reproducing cells [a] characteristic common to cancer cells

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:51.029
The tumor Shrinks as the cells stop dividing and die

00:02:52.750 --> 00:03:00.479
most chemotherapy drugs work systemically as they travel throughout your body in your bloodstream as they circulate the

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.990
drugs damaged metastatic cancer cells in other organs

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.279
unfortunately chemotherapy drugs cannot tell the difference between

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:14.909
Fast-growing normal cells and cancer cells as a result these drugs also damage

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:19.740
Or irritate some of your fast-growing normal cells such as those in your bone marrow

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.260
digestive system and Hair follicles

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:32.649
Death Irritation or damage to these normal cells produces [side-effects] such [as] a weakened immune system

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.140
Nausea and Hair loss

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:44.760
the goal of Chemotherapy is to reduce or eliminate cancer cells in the original tumor and any sites of

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.210
Metastasis

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:52.619
In addition to being a primary cancer treatment doctors often use chemotherapy as a secondary treatment

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:58.589
before during or after other primary cancer treatments such as [radiation] therapy or

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.040
surgical excision of a tumor

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:09.749
Depending on the location and type of [cancer] you may receive chemotherapy drugs intended to circulate throughout your body

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.650
including pills

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.220
capsules or liquids taken orally and

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.109
Intravenous or intramuscular

00:04:17.109 --> 00:04:19.109
injections

00:04:19.209 --> 00:04:23.488
Alternatively you may receive drugs delivered only to the area of the tumor

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:29.370
One local method delivers drugs to your bladder or chest through narrow Tubes called Catheters

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:36.809
Another local method injects drugs into the cerebrospinal fluid surrounding your brain and spinal Cord

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:44.330
A third local method places slowly dissolving wafers into an area where a tumor was removed

00:04:46.199 --> 00:04:51.508
In most cases you will receive a number of different chemotherapy drugs to increase their effectiveness

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:57.239
[you] may receive many chemotherapy treatments spread out over a period of weeks or months?

00:04:57.909 --> 00:05:04.139
This allows your body to recover between treatments and to kill as many cancer cells as possible

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:11.439
common side effects of chemotherapy include hair loss nausea

00:05:12.259 --> 00:05:13.909
decreased appetite

00:05:13.909 --> 00:05:15.909
fatigue anemia

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.900
bruising and

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.790
diarrhea

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.660
It is important to rest

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:28.939
Eat Nutritious foods and take medications prescribed by your doctor to reduce or minimize these side-effects

